{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"610cd852-007b-4100-95f3-d9811af8382e","runId":"24cb4b26-0b7d-4d67-a8ac-67eed4b33462","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":9,"previousEventHash":"sha256:fb3e7f70a4f3d0e812cb57d35a9d345feb4a953edc74bb13ee3f43b84ff25e5b","type":"node.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a039fc-a8fa-798e-be67-c2073dbf37fd","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-25T18:10:12.390Z","idempotencyKey":"node:investigate-1:completed","payload":{"nodeId":"investigate-1","node":"investigate","attempt":1,"round":1,"headSha":"03e6133becc50ba8509b976743ea76ffeaab2c4d","baseSha":"03e6133becc50ba8509b976743ea76ffeaab2c4d","outcome":"decomposed","verificationResults":[],"evidence":["`src/agents/child-runtime.ts:493-538` executes an approved verification argv directly with the assigned worktree as cwd; it does not enforce container UID/GID, redirect project caches, or inspect ownership after the command.","`src/agents/child-runtime.ts:1525-1550` relocates HOME/XDG configuration to a temporary directory, but this does not stop Docker bind-mounted repository paths from receiving root-owned pytest/runtime artifacts.","`src/adapters/git.ts:267-300` removes generated runtime, checks Git cleanliness, invokes `git worktree remove` as the host process, and only then attempts recursive `rm`; an ownership permission error is not classified as already absent and therefore aborts cleanup before fallback or local branch deletion.","`src/adapters/git.ts:319-335` cleans only ForgeDock-generated `.pi` paths and has no scan, diagnosis, ownership normalization, or supported remediation for foreign-owned ignored artifacts elsewhere in the worktree.","`src/workflows/orchestrate.ts:224-270` and `src/workflows/work-on.ts:2104-2117` show cancellation stops active subagents and records cancellation but does not schedule or invoke owned-worktree cleanup.","`test/adapters/git.test.ts:39-113` covers successful and idempotent cleanup with host-owned files only; there is no permission/foreign-owner regression coverage."]}}
